                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "well i downloaded this Nihilist Simulator last night at 3am instead of sleeping again. figured why the fuck not, everything is pointless anyway.\ngame is literally you sitting in a dark room, clicking on stuff, reading depressing texts about how nothing matters, your life is empty, achievements are fake, etc. sometimes you go outside, get hit by a car or talk to a girl who instantly ghosts you. pretty accurate tbh.\nthe humor is black as my soul. some lines genuinely made me exhale through my nose. the soundtrack is just sad rain and low piano, which fits perfectly. i beat it in one sitting (like 40 minutes) while eating cold pizza and feeling nothing.\nits not really a game tho. more like an interactive shitpost about existence. after finishing it i just stared at the wall for 10 minutes and then opened cs2 to die to russians like usual. nothing changed.\nwould i recommend? idk man. if youre a depressed 27 year old virgin who already knows life is meaningless — you’ll probably relate and get a couple dark chuckles. if you want actual gameplay go play something else.\nexistence is pain but at least this one was free on sale. whatever.",
